The search→rate delay is clear. I'm ready to write up the findings.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS client_p50_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS server_p50_ms, avg(c.duration - s.duration)/1e6 AS gap_avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "search's rate.GetRates calls take about 1.95 s at p50, while rate's server span takes under 1 ms; roughly 1.96 s is added between them."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS client_p50_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS server_p50_ms FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "In the normal period the same search-to-rate call has client and server p50 of about 1.6 ms and 0.9 ms."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name, c.span_name, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS client_p50_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS server_p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='frontend' AND c.span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "frontend's search.Search/Nearby client p50 is about 1950 ms, matching search's server span, so the delay passes straight up from search to frontend."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

